filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-11-08: doctrenderer's
editors.cpp does not tell the PDF editor's drawing file its CMap folder in
a WebAssembly build.

From 10.0 (v10.0.0.169), editors.cpp, as it puts together the scripts a
JavaScript engine would run, calls CDrawingFile::SetCMapFolder, which sets
a static member defined in drawingfile.cpp. That file is the PDF editor's
part of doctrenderer, which 01-cryptpad-wasm.patch leaves out with the
JavaScript engine (doctrenderer here runs no scripts; CryptPad's stand-ins
answer for it), so x2t's link stopped: "undefined symbol:
CDrawingFile::m_sCMapFolder" (measured). Under __EMSCRIPTEN__ the call is
left out; nothing in this build reads the folder.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

diff --git a/DesktopEditor/doctrenderer/editors.cpp b/DesktopEditor/doctrenderer/editors.cpp
index ea973d68..2d9dcd2a 100644
--- a/DesktopEditor/doctrenderer/editors.cpp
+++ b/DesktopEditor/doctrenderer/editors.cpp
@@ -115,7 +115,9 @@ namespace NSDoctRenderer
 #endif
 
 			std::wstring sCachePath = L"";
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
